A||N||14||87ECO5||Anyone here seeing (or did see at one time) a Psychiatrist?||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||04-20-2001||12:30 PM||||Anyone here willing to admit this?  Why did you go?  Did it help with whatever your problem was?  Is it expensive?  How long did you go?<P>Let's just say I feel like my mind is tied in a knot and I need someone to get that knot out.<P>Any information is greatly appreciated.<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||KnightRyder31||04-20-2001||12:48 PM||||I am my own Psychiatrist.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||04-20-2001||01:46 PM||||I've been through it.  I only did it for a little while though.  I don't like medicine, and I especially don't like people who try to give me medicine.  That was a big turn off to me.  <P>But I say go for it.  The worst that can happen is that it won't help, but there is a tremendous upside to it. I got friends who have gone or are still going to therapy, and it has helped some tremdnousley, and hasn't helped others at all.  But if you go in with a positive attitude, and an honest willingness to change, I think it can be a huge help.  <BR>Just my 2cents||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||04-20-2001||02:02 PM||||Definately no shame in getting help for mental/emotional issues. I myself have dealt often with clinical depression and lost an older brother to mental illness. The main step is to recognize that you need help. Seeking it out isn't that hard. Financial burdens should never keep you from getting help. Contact your local mental health department (sitting in the lobby of county mental health will make you feel extremely sane, in comparison) or talk to your clergy. The key in my experience is that all dark thoughts lose their power when they are brought into the light.<P>"stimpy saw a shrink? Now there's a shocker!"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steve Normington||04-20-2001||04:22 PM||||I did, it helped tremendously. Hate taking medication, but it's better than the alternative.<P>------------------<BR>85 SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||04-20-2001||08:33 PM||||Scott--Email me.<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000006||deceler8||04-20-2001||08:57 PM||||Three words...<P>St. John's Wort.<P>I'm a stock trader and I haven't killed myself during the past year, so the stuff must work.<P>Seriously...give it a try. It's hard to describe how it helps...I find I'm able to maintain perspective and think clearly. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Taijiguy||04-20-2001||09:57 PM||||I talked to one for a few months. It was couples stuff mostly, looking to improve our relationship. (It didn't work, and it was all my ex's fault  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">) The woman we saw was OK at helping to identify issues, but she was no good at providing "tools" to deal with things.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||04-20-2001||10:39 PM||||Well, I'll throw out a disclaimer right off the bat.  I have a low opinion of the mental health industry as a whole due to some bad experiences with some family members.  That having been said, I do believe counseling can do wonders.  I'm leary of Dr.'s who just want to subscribe medicine to make you feel "correct."  <P>For me, my friends are my therapists.  We talk about our problems and get stuff off our chest.  It helps quite a bit.  But sometimes you need to talk to a professional.  I would check clinics that are free or state supported.  In my experience, the people who work there seem to care more, overall, than those who work in the nice, expensive clinics and hospitals.  Those people seem to just be there for the money.  A lot of people in state run or state supported clinics do it because they believe in what they do.<P>And did you ever notice that Therapist is spelled The-rapist?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000009||Raydar||04-21-2001||10:39 AM||||Okay. I'm seeing a common theme here. <BR>"I don't want someone to fill me full of drugs."<P>Go and see a Psychologist, instead of a Psychiatrist. <BR>A Psychologist does <I>not</I> prescribe drugs. He/she merely councils, and helps you to see what you need to see. They are very skillful, though. <BR>I saw one for just a few months. (All I needed.) I'd recommend it highly. YMMV.<BR>Why did I go? Anxiety/panic attacks.<BR>Thought I was having heart attacks. Scary.<BR>-------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-21-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000010||Jaygee79||04-21-2001||03:33 PM||||I went to a psychologist for a long time after my parents got divorced.  I liked it.  Talking to someone neutral really helps.  Don't know how expensive it is, my mother paid.<P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooheey1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jaygee79 (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000011||Mach10||04-21-2001||06:01 PM||||Unless you are having some serious, serious psychosomatic issues, a pshychiatrist probably insn't what you want. A Psychologist will more likely be the helpful one. Psychiatry is treating the brain, while a psychologist treats the mind. Psychologists cannot prescribe medication, but if it is warranted, will refer you to someone that will. Been there, done that, learned to cope without the meds. <BR>||||reg||7
Z||000012||Bluebottlejunky||04-21-2001||06:04 PM||||ya, I went for a wile when I was little because of my parents divorce..I really didn't like it at all I would go nuts when I had to go..but that went away..and in the long run it did help.<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||3
Z||000013||JSocha||04-23-2001||12:58 PM||||If you read enough of these threads, over time you may come to the realization that your problems aren't as big as others!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Seriously though, I went (was forced) to see both a Psycologist (15 years ago) and then a Psycharistrist (6 years back).<P>I personally wasn't impressed with either, especially the Psychatrist.  Started prescribing every medication under the sun and I didn't feel myself and quit them and resolved the issues myself and started feeling alot better...now where did I put that Uzi?<P>Psycologist, well, she was darn good looking and I just enjoyed sitting on the chair across from her, discussing things just for the visit with her and letting my imagination run wild.  18 year old hormones at work of course!  Helped quite a bit cause I always went out of the session with a smile on my face and she thought it was because of our discussion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  However, I didn't feel she really helped me with the problem as I couldn't blame my problems on anybody else...had to take responsibility for every action.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Phaeton||04-24-2001||02:59 AM||||Shrinks are people too, and if there is no common ground not much will happen.  But the next one may change your world.<P>They all have information, the need is to connect to the person that can communicate that knowledge to you in usable form.<P>Luck||||reg||12
